[Music]  attendance continues to be a concern in  our schools the school district  struggled to reach its goal in reducing  student absences last year the question  this year are things any better some  parents tell candace charles the first  day of school not a good sign candace  joined us live in studio to tell us why  families are blaming the district  yeah let's say class schedules not being  done student is not registered the list  goes on for a number of reasons students  are already missing school but district  is working to improve intended we were  very disappointed she was looking  forward to her first day at school  instead sabrina calisco's sister katie  keene was told to go home we were told  that her packet was ready she had  everything that she needed to be  registered in the school i just hadn't  been processed yet there are 295 000  students enrolled in the school district  with issues the first week of school  some were on the way to becoming a  chronic absentee student it only takes  missing 18 days or more to get the  designation katie already missed two  she's been sitting in the library into  her sixth period because they still had  not made her  a schedule some of the reasons students  missed school no class schedule to  shared housing issues did not explain  why it hadn't been processed they just  simply  said that  they were overwhelmed when we were in  line they were just sending kids home  left and right last year according to  ccsd the chronic absenteeism rate was  just shy of 34 percent a little higher  than the states and neighboring  districts johnson middle school where  katie attends sat at 51 percent the  result of all this missed class time  causing backlash for the district i  personally went to ccsd my sisters go to  ccsd my son will not be going to ccsd if  first week of school is this much of a  disaster  i'm not interested in putting my son in  ccsd  now a district representative told me  quote in general we are working on  things side by side with schools to  approve attendance it currently has 25  truancy officers but they couldn't give  me exact reasons or numbers on those  recent absences for now in the studio  i'm kandace charles 8 news now candace  thank you and in 2019 the district set a  goal in its five-year strategic plan to  reduce chronic absenteeism to 16 in 2024  the district continues to work towards  that goal

